  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Just energy transition: accelerating access to clean energy in Botswana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Botswana needs an increased uptake of renewable energy to address domestic energy demand, especially in rural areas. The proposed joint programme (JP) will demonstrate how a systems approach based on the principles of circular economy can be utilised in implementing Just Energy Transition. The project will demonstrate use of biogas in schools and use of bio-slurry to organically fertilize back-yard gardens, with a potential for upscaling, in nearby communities.  New green and decent jobs will be created therefore, reducing the opportunity costs associated with the long hours spent by women and girls collecting fuelwood. A clean cooking roadmap will be developed,with the aim to understand the current state of energy access and its implications on both the environment and public health. The JP will also enhance the meaningful engagement of young people in just energy transition through education, innovation and participation in local and global advocacy. The JP is expected to accelerate the achievement of Botswana#s SDG goals: increasing food security, improving nutrition and promoting sustainable agriculture (SDG2) opening the pathways towards increasing access to modern, affordable and clean energy (SDG7) and promoting development-oriented policies leading to decent job creation and innovation (SDG8), while int</narrative>
  </description>
